Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 19:38:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 049/154] feat: auto-peek's throttle comes back, on the Rust
 answer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The throttle, ShouldAutoPeek and OpenAutoPeek were all removed with the ABI,
not just re-pointed - the task description said the registration survived, and
it had not.

ShouldAutoPeek fills PeekDecisionInputs from live objects and asks
atrium_core_is_peek_source_url for the one field Swift used to answer. It asks
LAST, and only when the cheap fields already agree, because that call takes the
core's lock and walks the active space. The profile id is derived the way
BrowserController derives its own cached one, so no accessor had to be opened
up.

MaybeCreateAndAdd no longer gates on anything. It used to refuse to register
without a dylib export; a statically linked core cannot be absent, so the
content-side gates carry the per-navigation cost instead.

Registered under BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC), the same footprint as the rest of atrium/.

A throttle now runs on every navigation, so the check that mattered before
commit was that ordinary navigation still works: sidebar-row-click 3 of 3,
which opens a cross-site tab, and devtools-dock 2 of 2.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc | 8 ++++++++
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn                      | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
index 356faf9cbdbe6..71154cffec88c 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -180,6 +180,9 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/task_manager/task_manager_interface.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/tracing/chrome_tracing_delegate.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/translate/translate_service.h"
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
+#include "chrome/browser/ui/atrium/atrium_peek_navigation_throttle.h"
+#endif
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/blocked_content/blocked_window_params.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/blocked_content/chrome_popup_navigation_delegate.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_id.h"
@@ -5664,6 +5667,11 @@ void ChromeContentBrowserClient::RemovePresentationObserver(
 void ChromeContentBrowserClient::CreateThrottlesForNavigation(
     content::NavigationThrottleRegistry& registry) {
   CreateAndAddChromeThrottlesForNavigation(registry);
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
+  // Auto-peek. An off-site link click from a pinned or favourited
+  // tab opens the Keyhole instead of navigating that tab away.
+  atrium::AtriumPeekNavigationThrottle::MaybeCreateAndAdd(registry);
+#endif
 }
 
